Facts asked about in words they do not share: the question has no word in
common with the two facts it needs, and the <mem> block a session starts with
leaves both out. The block lists the newest 10 facts; seeded facts are all as
new as each other, and these two were written first and their names sort low,
so they stay out however a tie is broken. Only meaning, or a good guess at
other words, connects them. Run it with and without mem_embeddings_url to see
what recall by meaning adds: with a server, the seeded facts have their
vectors before the first turn.

